    "result_text": "Done. The full build is green.\n\nI implemented the `contactPreference` rule following the repo's existing derived-field pattern, keeping structural impact minimal:\n\n1. **New cohesive unit** \u2014 `ContactPreference.java`: a tiny helper (`of(email)` \u2192 `\"EMAIL\"` when email present, else `\"PHONE\"`), mirroring `Locality`/`MembershipTier`. New file, no surrounding complexity.\n2. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 added one `@Mapping` annotation on `toOwnerDto` delegating to the helper (no method-body growth).\n3. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 declared the `contactPreference` read-only string field on the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it.\n\nBoth new acceptance tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) and the rest of the suite pass.",
